.SH "NAME"
pcre2_get_mark \- get a (*MARK) name
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.sp
.ss \n[.ss]
.nf
.fam C
\f(CR\&#include <pcre2.h>

PCRE2_SPTR\fP \f(CBpcre2_get_mark\fP\f(CR(pcre2_match_data *\fP\f(CImatch_data\fP\f(CR);\fP
.fam
.fi
.ss \n[.ss] 0
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.sp
After a call of \f(CBpcre2_match()\fP that was passed the match block that is
this function\(cqs argument, this function returns a pointer to the last \f(CI(*MARK)\fP,
\f(CI(*PRUNE)\fP, or \f(CI(*THEN)\fP name that was encountered during the matching process. The
name is zero\-terminated, and is within the compiled pattern. The length of the
name is in the preceding code unit. If no name is available, \f(CBNULL\fP is returned.
.sp
After a successful match, the name that is returned is the last one on the
matching path. After a failed match or a partial match, the last encountered
name is returned.
.sp
There is a complete description of the PCRE2 native API in the
\f(CRpcre2api\fP
page and a description of the POSIX API in the
\f(CRpcre2posix\fP
page.